From: Jason Stanko <jstanko@google.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:42:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] profile: Cap oFono HFP HF version to 1.6

Debian Bookworm's oFono 1.31 reads the negotiated HFP profile version
from BlueZ's Profile1.NewConnection properties. When the peer advertises
HFP 1.7 (0x0107), oFono sets HFP_HF_FEATURE_HF_INDICATORS (AT+BRSF=511),
but its cmer_cb() in drivers/hfpmodem/slc.c only checks for 3-way
calling and jumps straight to slc_established() without sending AT+BIND
when the AG does not advertise 3-way calling. Floss strictly waits for
AT+BIND when both sides negotiate HF Indicators and times out SLC setup
after 5 seconds.

Cap oFono's external HFP HF profile (/bluetooth/profile/hfp_hf) to HFP
1.6 (0x0106) on registration and in send_new_connection(). This keeps
stock Debian oFono 1.31 negotiating HFP 1.6 (AT+BRSF=255, with WBS mSBC
intact) while leaving PipeWire's HFP 1.9 SWB profile (/Profile/HFPHF)
untouched.
---
 src/profile.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

--- a/src/profile.c
+++ b/src/profile.c
@@ -1050,6 +1050,13 @@ static bool send_new_connection(struct ext_profile *ext, struct ext_io *conn)
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (!g_strcmp0(ext->path, "/bluetooth/profile/hfp_hf") &&
+			ext->version && conn->version > ext->version) {
+		DBG("Capping %s peer version from 0x%04x to 0x%04x",
+			ext->path, conn->version, ext->version);
+		conn->version = ext->version;
+	}
+
 	dbus_message_iter_init_append(msg, &iter);
 
 	path = device_get_path(conn->device);
@@ -2375,6 +2382,19 @@ static struct ext_profile *create_ext(const char *owner, const char *path,
 		dbus_message_iter_next(opts);
 	}
 
+	/* Debian Bookworm's oFono 1.31 advertises HFP 1.7 (HF Indicators) in
+	 * AT+BRSF=511 when negotiated with version 0x0107, but its cmer_cb()
+	 * skips AT+BIND when the AG does not support 3-way calling, causing
+	 * Floss to time out SLC setup. Cap oFono's HFP HF profile to 1.6
+	 * without affecting PipeWire (/Profile/HFPHF) HFP 1.9 SWB.
+	 */
+	if (!g_strcmp0(ext->path, "/bluetooth/profile/hfp_hf") &&
+			ext->version > 0x0106) {
+		info("Capping %s HFP version from 0x%04x to 0x0106",
+			ext->path, ext->version);
+		ext->version = 0x0106;
+	}
+
 	if (!ext->service)
 		set_service(ext);
 
-- 
